    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "Convergence of go‑mHC is governed by the geometry of the loss landscape introduced by manifold M and gradient stability; go‑mHC is expected to have learnable gradients, be convergent, and fully connected (able to reach any target matrix). See Appendix B.7 for proofs.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000098"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [
        "Section 5 Convergence"
      ],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "Not all matrix parameterizations are learnable and fully connected; mHC‑lite may suffer from vanishing gradients, making it difficult to relearn an n‑stream transform after convergence. See Appendix B.10.",
